   $q$Which statement best expresses a central theme of the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Mentors exist mainly to find the mistakes that students make in their experiments.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-character"},{"text":"Mold grows at the same rate on bread whether or not the bread is treated with cloves.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-theme"},{"text":"Students should choose research questions that are certain to produce exciting results.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Reporting disappointing results honestly can turn a failed experiment into something useful to others.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Reporting disappointing results honestly can turn a failed experiment into something useful to others.$q$, $q$Halima's honest poster of a negative result proves valuable to the graduate student, which carries the theme. The clove and mold choice states a finding of the experiment, not a message about life or work.$q$, 'draft', '6e07af05-c302-5308-bdee-146ba797d760')
