   $q$How do the bridge image in the fifth stanza and the final stanza work together to deepen the theme?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They shift the poem's subject from family to engineering and road building.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"They show the speaker's pride mixed with loss as the father grows independent, then reveal that the two now depend on each other.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They show that the father no longer needs any help and the family's struggles are over.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-ending"},{"text":"They show that the speaker resents the father's progress and wants him to stay dependent.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstates-claim"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They show the speaker's pride mixed with loss as the father grows independent, then reveal that the two now depend on each other.$q$, $q$The bridge carrying "traffic you did not send" captures pride shaded by feeling less needed, and the final stanza shows each checking the other's work, so the helping now runs both ways. The speaker says "I am proud of him," so resentment overstates the feeling.$q$, 'draft', '03aa796a-0ab7-593c-a290-c6cc033d038e')
